   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Detail, manual mask (FLUX 3 Klein)** - ADetailer-style \"inpaint only masked\"\n\n1. Load the image in **Image to fix**, right-click it > **Open in MaskEditor**, paint over what you want redone (a face, a hand, a sword hilt) and **Save**.\n2. Separate painted blobs become separate regions. A painted outline is filled in.\n3. Describe the region in the prompt if the default doesn't fit (\"a steel sword hilt wrapped in leather\").\n\n**Settings (Detailer node)**\n- **denoise**: 0.3 keeps nearly everything, **0.4 default**, 0.5-0.6 redraws more (fixes broken hands/faces, may drift).\n- **guide_size 1024 / crop_region**: each region (with context) is enlarged so its short side is 1024 px, long side capped by **max_size** (1536). Klein's sweet spot is about 1 MP.\n- **feather** / **noise_mask_feather**: softness of the paste-back seam and of the repaint edge.\n- **cycle 2**: a second pass on the result; sometimes cleaner, twice as slow.\n- Multiple separate regions are done one after another; seed + 1 for each.\n\n**References**: *Reference 1* is fed to Klein for every region, so a face stays the face in the reference. The prompt refers to it as `<ref_image_0>` (and `<ref_image_1>` for Reference 2). No reference? Bypass Reference 1 (Ctrl+B) and drop the sentence with `<ref_image_0>` from the prompt.\n\n**Mask to regions**: *crop_factor* = context around each region (2.5 = 2.5x its size); *drop_size* skips tiny blobs.\n\n*Regions before/after* show each crop; *Before / after* the whole image. Output: `output/detail/`. Transparency is not kept.\n"
   ],
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Tailored for this setup"
  }
